{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1028001-shapeshifting-hedge-wizard-versus-shapeshifting-revised","id":1028001,"title":"Shapeshifting (Hedge Wizard) versus Shapeshifting (Revised)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T20:20:20-08:00","id":1028001,"title":"Shapeshifting (Hedge Wizard) versus Shapeshifting (Revised)","content":"I am curious which version of the Numina of Shapeshifting people thought was more powerful/unbalanced? I will give a summation of the capabilities at level 5, the maximum level that a beginning sorcerer could start with, so that people who are unfamiliar with Sorcerer: The Hedge Wizard's Handbook and Sorcerer: Revised can participate in the discussion. For the purpose of clarity, Shapeshifting (Hedge Wizard) produces permanent changes that may only be reversed by spending a point of Willpower, casting another Shapeshifting spell, or Unweaving Countermagic while Shapeshifting (Revised) produces temporary changes that last only a scene.<br /> <br /> Hedge Wizard Version<br /> -Practitioners gain an automatic bonus to social dice pools equal to five dice.<br /> -Practitioners may shapeshift to increase one physical attribute by up to three dice.<br /> -Practitioners may shapeshift into any existent animal, from the size of a mouse to the size of an elephant, that they can study, though they risk losing their mind to their animal side (Willpower roll, difficulty 6, to avoid).<br /> <br /> Revised Version<br /> -Practitioners may shapeshift into any animal as long as it is not mythical (so dinosaurs are a possibility).<br /> -Practitioners may shapeshift two of their allies into any type of animal as long as it is not mythical (once again, dinosaurs are a possibility).<br /> -Practitioners may shapeshift two of their enemies into any type of animal, as long as it is not mythical, without the possible of resistance (except if their enemy possesses a form of Countermagic), even if their enemies are supernatural creatures like Changelings or Vampires.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like both versions for different reasons, and I use them in my campaigns. I change the Hedge Wizard version into Shapeshifting (Personal) and the Revised version into Shapeshifting (Peripheral). I am just wondering which versions other people preferred","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T15:31:38-08:00","id":1028712,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to remember some of the things we did... longer ago than I care to admit. A lot was modified by Paradigm. I.E., Dr Moreau never changed himself, and it was always permanent. Jekyll was exactly the opposite.<br /> <br /> Some constants: social bonuses were like any other attribute boost, and required a spell. Bonus was just overpowered otherwise.<br /> <br /> There were a variety of ways to resist. Vampires could 'heal' it like higher gen Vic mods. Those with Protean or Vic could resist directly. <br /> <br /> WtA style Shapeshifters could 'soak' it out of Breed form, and shapeshifting undid the changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}